/target/
/out/

# Installer-managed AI tooling. `npx bmad-method install` writes the planning workflow's
# agent definitions into whichever editors you select, and they are reinstalled rather than
# committed -- see CONTRIBUTING.md. Vendoring them would mean carrying hundreds of generated
# files that the installer replaces on its next run.
#
# Ignored here rather than left untracked, for a specific reason: the publication-hygiene
# gate refuses to publish these paths, so a `git add -A` after installing would produce a
# commit that CI rejects. The gate is right to refuse and stays as it is; this keeps the
# situation from arising.
/_bmad/
/.claude/
/.cursor/
/.agents/
/.agent/
/.Codex/
/.cursorrules.local

# The planning archive under `_bmad-output/` is NOT ignored. It is committed source, and the
# leading slash above matters: `_bmad/` is the tooling, `_bmad-output/` is the work product.
